menu "Aleph One PC card (!PC)"

config ALEPHPC_APCDISK
	tristate "!PC's hard discs and swap device (apcdisk)"
	depends on X86_32 && BLOCK && ISA
	help
	  The hard discs (HD0, HD1) and swap device that Aleph One's !PC
	  gives the PC card, as /dev/apda, /dev/apdb and /dev/apdc, through
	  !PC's HPC calls.

config ALEPHPC_APCNET
	bool "The fast path to !PC's NE2000 (apcnet)"
	depends on X86_32 && NET && ISA
	help
	  !PC 3.09's fast path to its NE2000 (PCNE2): frames go through
	  rings in the PC's memory rather than the 8390's data port, one
	  mailbox access for each frame sent or batch received rather than
	  one for each word. When !PC has it, this driver takes the NE2000's
	  ports so that ne.c leaves the card alone; when !PC hasn't, ne.c
	  drives the NE2000 as before. apcnet.disable=1 leaves it to ne.c.

endmenu
